  "sn12.70:16.1": "The word “every” here and in all parallel passages is <i>sabba,</i> which is the same as the word for “all.” On the range of meaning covered by the word “all,” see <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn35.23'>SN 35:23</a>. <a href='https://suttacentral.net/dn11'>DN 11</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/dn15'>DN 15</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn49'>MN 49</a>, and <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an10.81'>AN 10:81</a> indicate that there is a type of consciousness that lies outside the range of “all,” and so would not fall under the aggregate of consciousness. This apparently corresponds to the dimension mentioned in <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn35.117'>SN 35:117</a> and <a href='https://suttacentral.net/ud8.1'>Ud 8:1</a>.",
  "sn12.70:16.2": "",
